WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.413 --> 00:00:03.213
(bouncy, cheerful music)

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:07.130
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.630
- [Narrator] Look familiar?

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.070
Welcome to the garden of
none other than Claude Monet,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.970
the father of French impressionism.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.670
Worldwide renowned painter who planted

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.640
his own garden here in Giverny in 1883,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.793
and replicated it time and
time again on canvases.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:45.940
And this is Gilbert.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.420
He's an artist in his own right.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.250
He has been responsible for the upkeep

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.763
of Monet's garden for over 40 years.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.160
After the second World War,

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.050
the garden was left neglected.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.243
So in the 1970s, gardeners
were called to the rescue.

00:01:04.776 --> 00:01:08.693
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:03.444 --> 00:02:05.940
Gilbert wasn't the greatest
connoisseur of Monet,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.420
but he got to know him through his garden.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.337
(speaking in foreign language)

